Q7. What is Docker Build Context?

Interview Ready Answer

The Docker Build Context is the set of files and directories that Docker
can access during the image build process. When the docker build command
is executed, Docker sends the specified directory (build context) to the
Docker daemon, allowing Dockerfile instructions such as COPY and ADD to
use those files.

Definition

Docker Build Context
- Directory supplied to docker build.
- Contains Dockerfile, source code, configuration files, and other
  required resources.

Purpose

• Makes project files available during image creation.
• Required for COPY and ADD instructions.

